// APE ATOLL IS HOSTILE TO ANYTHING THAT IS NOT A MONKEY, and until now it was hostile to nothing.
//
// Not one npc on the island or in Zooknock's tunnel carried a huntmode, so the monkey guards, the
// archers on the walkways, the gorillas and the zombies all stood and watched the player walk past
// - and walk through them, since nothing that never attacks ever gets in your way. Reported from
// play as "nothing is agro on island or in tunnel" and "monkeys dont shoot arrows at u".
//
// THE GREEGREE IS WHAT STOPS THEM. That is the whole point of the quest: Zooknock carves you a
// monkey and the island stops seeing an intruder. So these are shaped on [aggressive_melee] and
// [aggressive_ranged] from the 377 cache - same visibility, same combat guards - with one addition
// borrowed from the God Wars dungeon, where "aggressive unless you are wearing their god's item"
// has the same shape: check_invparam=worn,mm_transmog_npc,<1 means "hunt only when nothing WORN
// carries the transmogrification param", and every greegree carries it (quest_mm.param).
//
// Worn, not inv: carrying a greegree in your pack is not wearing a monkey's face, and the quest
// makes you wield it.
//
// check_nottoostrong is off, like the cache's own aggressive pair: Ape Atoll does not care how
// high your combat level is, which is the island's reputation and the reason the quest tells you
// to bring the greegree rather than a weapon.

[mm_aggressive_melee]
type=player
check_vis=lineofsight
check_nottoostrong=off
check_notcombat=%lastcombat
check_notcombat_self=%npc_lastcombat
check_notbusy=off
check_invparam=worn,mm_transmog_npc,<1
find_keephunting=off
find_newmode=opplayer2

[mm_aggressive_ranged]
type=player
check_vis=lineofsight
check_nottoostrong=off
check_notcombat=%lastcombat
check_notcombat_self=%npc_lastcombat
check_notbusy=off
check_invparam=worn,mm_transmog_npc,<1
find_keephunting=off
find_newmode=applayer2
